CREOracleRecovery
├── A guard can directly apply the latest authenticated rejected report
│   ├── Recovery updates valuation without another forwarder delivery
│   ├── Unseen reports cannot be approved
│   ├── Malformed bytes and changes to any cached report field cannot authorize recovery
│   ├── A newer rejected report replaces the candidate without pausing active NAV
│   ├── Invalid destinations and snapshots cannot replace the cached candidate
│   ├── Candidates at or before the active snapshot cannot be reviewed
│   └── A newer candidate remains reviewable after an older report becomes active
├── Later reports can replace the active valuation after a deviation rejection
│   ├── Raised movement limits allow a later report without curator intervention
│   ├── Unchanged limits compare the later report with the active valuation
│   ├── Rejection preserves cash and liquidity while acceptance prevents reviewing the older candidate
│   └── Rejected reports preserve active NAV and allow intervening capital flows
├── Candidate handling preserves active accounting
│   ├── Empty reports cannot clear the candidate or change the accepted snapshot
│   ├── Workflow cutover preserves active accounting and the cached candidate remains reviewable
│   └── Delayed review preserves the snapshot block and allows the next completed snapshot
└── Direct recovery retains all non-movement checks
    ├── Report review allows any elapsed delay
    ├── Invalid or nonadvancing snapshot blocks preserve the candidate
    └── Insufficient liquidity defers settlement and later cash waits for its covering report
